.TH "PERIODICWAVE.PERIODICWAVE" "3JS" "October 28, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
PeriodicWave.PeriodicWave \- PeriodicWave: PeriodicWave() constructor
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]PeriodicWave()\f[B]\f[R] constructor of the Web Audio API
creates a new \f[CR]PeriodicWave\f[R] object instance.
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
new PeriodicWave(context)
new PeriodicWave(context, options)
.EE
.SS Parameters
.TP
\f[B]context\f[R]
A \f[CR]BaseAudioContext\f[R] representing the audio context you want
the node to be associated with.
.TP
\f[B]options\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
A \c
.UR https://webaudio.github.io/web-audio-api/#idl-def-PeriodicWaveOptions
\f[CR]PeriodicWaveOptions\f[R]
.UE \c
\ dictionary object defining the properties you want the
\f[CR]PeriodicWave\f[R] to have (It also inherits the options defined in
the \c
.UR https://webaudio.github.io/web-audio-api/#idl-def-PeriodicWaveConstraints
PeriodicWaveConstraints
.UE \c
\ dictionary.):
.RS
.TP
\f[B]real\f[R]
A \f[CR]Float32Array\f[R] containing the cosine terms that you want to
use to form the wave (equivalent to the \f[CR]real\f[R] parameter of
\f[CR]BaseAudioContext.createPeriodicWave\f[R]).
.TP
\f[B]imag\f[R]
A \f[CR]Float32Array\f[R] containing the sine terms that you want to use
to form the wave (equivalent to the \f[CR]imag\f[R] parameter of
\f[CR]BaseAudioContext.createPeriodicWave\f[R]).
.RE
.SS Return value
A new \f[CR]PeriodicWave\f[R] object instance.
.SH EXAMPLES
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] real = \f[B]new\f[R] Float32Array(2);
\f[B]const\f[R] imag = \f[B]new\f[R] Float32Array(2);
\f[B]const\f[R] ac = \f[B]new\f[R] AudioContext();

real[0] = 0;
imag[0] = 0;
real[1] = 1;
imag[1] = 0;

\f[B]const\f[R] wave = \f[B]new\f[R] PeriodicWave(ac, {
  real,
  imag,
  disableNormalization: \f[B]false\f[R],
});
.EE
